DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     rreessoollvvccoonnff..ccoonnff is the configuration file for resolvconf(8).  The
     rreessoollvvccoonnff..ccoonnff file is a shell script that is sourced by resolvconf(8),
     meaning that rreessoollvvccoonnff..ccoonnff must contain valid shell commands.  Listed
     below are the standard rreessoollvvccoonnff..ccoonnff variables that may be set.  If the
     values contain whitespace, wildcards or other special shell characters,
     ensure they are quoted and escaped correctly.  See the rreeppllaaccee variable
     for an example on quoting.

     After updating this file, you may wish to run rreessoollvvccoonnff --uu to apply the
     new configuration.

     When a dynamically generated list is appended or prepended to, the whole
     is made unique where left-most wins.

